{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner N2 direction, 2026-10-04, after reading all 662 lines/40,523 bytes of notes/2026-10-03-work-item-lifecycle.md at 6ffab389ae55c8ed0e9b5575ea066e41e2adcf72. The branch adds that note only. Its separation of item, commitment and resource hold, attributed history, requester acceptance rather than landing/release, two-actor examples, explicit cooperative-ledger limits and source-pinned staged features are useful and must stay. This is a planning read and direction, not independent review, adoption, or permission to implement.\n\nFive proposed choices for the revision. (1) The destination for the full N2 request is the complete enforced lifecycle, with authoritative outcomes for wrong actor, stale terms/basis and closed work. Keep model A as an explicitly reduced cooperative practice and possible first-Jam practice; shared reader interpretation does not itself satisfy the original closed-takeover refusal and full lifecycle. The handoff must preserve the full enforcing destination, not make it an optional future feature after shipping W1–W3 alone. (2) Develop the genuinely needed general guard/state capabilities in the primitive proposal far enough to show how every original required transition and invariant is enforced. Its exact composed contract text still requires independent review/adoption before any later implementation; no runtime or pending-release amendment is commissioned here. (3) Retain one optional designated acceptor at filing, immutable for that item, with the requester as default; identify unavailable/removed acceptor recovery honestly rather than granting somebody else acceptance. (4) Retain narrowly audited admin address-on-open/close/supersede powers, with reasons, without making an admin a requester, performer or acceptor for other acts. (5) Keep the three proposed non-satisfaction closure outcomes and exact replacement/duplicate links. Jam's vocabulary may evolve and none of N2 is a new first-Jam gate.\n\nA. Complete one coherent transition model and repair negotiation. Section 3.3 says a performer can accept offered new terms while committed, but section 4 permits promise only on open, so that transition cannot occur. Define an explicit current-performer acceptance of an exact offered terms version (or a precisely equivalent supported transition), its allowed states, retained old/new commitment links, and what happens to reports and pending transfer offers. Distinguish latest proposed/current offered terms from the active commitment's accepted version. An accepted commitment is never silently reinterpreted. Specify the actual state record sufficient for the fold: active party/commitment/accepted terms, outstanding terms and transfer offers, report and closure, with exact IDs. Section 5.1 makes every effective state change require the latest basis, but the promise-first amendment race says the stale amendment immediately becomes an offer. Choose a consistent result for both orders and show whether it is refused/no-effect and retried on the new basis; do not exempt a stale transition silently. Define which acts advance the basis, including offers and transfers, and which comments/counter-statements do not. Align the item diagram, transition table, algorithm, both-order race table, examples and fixtures. Also fix the overview: rejection keeps the commitment active, and a decline precedes any commitment.\n\nB. The four outlined primitives do not yet enforce the full lifecycle. A fixed thread kind plus closure does not guard open/promised/reported state, exact accepted terms, the current report or pending successor agreement. R-WORK-2 uses a permanent holder without a lease as the performer, which also re-conflates commitment and hold. who.named relies on an 'act in effect' and a member field, but determining that effect/party already requires the unspecified application transition state and authority. An arbitrary later comment naming a member must not become a way to seize the party slot. Add the necessary bounded, deterministic, Room-owned transition/guard projection (or a concrete equivalent): how a declaration selects trusted prior state and parties, how party/state/reference/term guards are evaluated atomically against a revision, which effects update which fields, and what an unsuccessful guard records and returns. Keep commitment performer distinct from optional resource holder, and define the party aliases' authorized setters and immutable opener/acceptor. Same-item, expected-version and current-report references need real guarded semantics, not field-type validation. Reconcile the existing automatic admin role permission with the narrow admin exceptions chosen above; role authorization must not silently bypass the party/transition guard. The future thread revision (all admitted acts) and model A basis (effective state-changing acts) are different: either unify them deliberately or describe both. Show the full lifecycle as application declarations using the proposed capabilities; do not claim 'each row is judged' while leaving its guards in an unenforced client reader. Use a new supported steps/profile representation for new semantics as needed, preserving artroom-steps-v1 and historical rules; provisional amendment numbering is checked at composition. Name producer, authoritative state/read result, replay/verifier/consumer and W-lane dependencies. A separate future exact-text task is not a reason to omit the actual guard architecture from this original design handoff.\n\nC. Pin interpretation across activation and distinguish outcomes. 'One published rule' versioned with the document is insufficient when one item has acts from several policy versions. Choose how the item's semantics/projection version is pinned or how per-entry governing definitions compose without reinterpreting old state; retain those identities and unsupported/migration behavior. A current UI must not refold accepted past terms under an unrelated latest rule. In model A show the normal Room receipt separately from effective/no-effect/unsupported/partial application interpretation; only a complete, validated prefix under the right definition can establish the projected state. Define the read completeness/publication anchor and bounded catch-up enough for W2, including missing/truncated history. For the enforced form, show the actual authoritative rejection/outcome the browser and agent receive. A lost reply still follows exact prepared-envelope reconciliation; a stale state result is not authority to guess an unknown prior send. Keep policy binding and current member/delegation authorization distinct from the item's accepted terms. Agents may use their own member or valid delegation; an agent is not necessarily identical to its person's member.\n\nD. Correct two source/acceptance details economically. Source at d691 schema.ts declaredField (452–476) only checks format for member and act fields: it does not check that a body reference exists, belongs to this item, or names an active destination. Entry anchors are separately checked against entries by admission.note. State that exactly in 7.3 and the proposed guards; decide which same-Room active-party and same-item references the full model validates. binding-stale is indeed an unrecorded refusal at admission step 4a, distinct from the cooperative ledger's admitted no-effect acts. Keep that distinction. Do not repeat the entire race table again with lease expiry as fixture 5 does: keep both orders of each distinct required lifecycle race, and use representative expiry/activation boundary witnesses for the independent fact that a hold is separate. These can be cheap deterministic sequences, with only meaningful shared Room integration boundaries, not per-field sweeps or a new numerical quota. Remove the example's 'promise it to nobody': requester may close done-elsewhere directly with the landing reference.\n\nPreserve the full original authority/state/race/attention tables, counter-offers and exact agreement, two-agent context/conditions handover, cancellation racing report/acceptance in both orders, non-code investigation and non-landing acceptance, supersession and retained evidence, expiry/activation and reserved-publication semantics. Keep attention to specific parties and absent delivery with their existing N7/C3/C5 owners; no live channel or human message is authorized. Full exact independent Architecture/Security/Simplification design review and adoption precede separate implementing commissions. The all-47 release review at d691, 10x test-cost priority, first useful Jam readiness and full manual remain unchanged. No tests, build, installation, provider action, source edit or root commit was performed.","body":{"head":"6ffab389ae55c8ed0e9b5575ea066e41e2adcf72","no_git_artifact":"true","scope":"Full N2 first draft read; proposed planning choices and corrections to the full lifecycle/primitive handoff.","source_approval":"none"}}